{
  "case_id": "2005-04-1034",
  "document_hash": "37b89618981b80a0caaf7d4b1ce314974005bf49d3b6542218470df118511611",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37b89618981b80a0caaf7d4b1ce314974005bf49d3b6542218470df118511611",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37b89618981b-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:12 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37b89618981b80a0caaf7d4b1ce314974005bf49d3b6542218470df118511611",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37b89618981b-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This is a case of agency overreaching. In this case, the Corps and EPA pushed the very limits of congressional authority, contrary to the plain text of the act and without any clear indication Congress intended that result."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37b89618981b80a0caaf7d4b1ce314974005bf49d3b6542218470df118511611",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37b89618981b-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Couldn't you simply assume that anything that is discharged into a tributary ultimately goes where the tributary goes? Wouldn't it be enough to prove the discharge?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37b89618981b80a0caaf7d4b1ce314974005bf49d3b6542218470df118511611",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37b89618981b-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How do you define a tributary?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37b89618981b80a0caaf7d4b1ce314974005bf49d3b6542218470df118511611",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37b89618981b-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "After years of review by the State of Michigan and the Respondent, the record is very clear. Petitioners' wetland is hydrologically isolated from any navigable water of the United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37b89618981b80a0caaf7d4b1ce314974005bf49d3b6542218470df118511611",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37b89618981b-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If you look at Respondents' brief in their arguments to this Court, they first state, page 18, that in fact traditionally they've looked at hydrological connection."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37b89618981b80a0caaf7d4b1ce314974005bf49d3b6542218470df118511611",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37b89618981b-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What is a hydrological connection? Is it enough if the water seeps through the ground and underground is connected with the navigable water, or does there have to be a ditch or -- or a culvert that you can see the water flowing through?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37b89618981b80a0caaf7d4b1ce314974005bf49d3b6542218470df118511611",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37b89618981b-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The sole reason claimed for jurisdiction at the agency hearing was adjacency to this non-navigable, unnamed ditch, which was dug by the county for a sewer system. That's the sole reason."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37b89618981b80a0caaf7d4b1ce314974005bf49d3b6542218470df118511611",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37b89618981b-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "if there's no hydrological connection today, but there would be after you -- after you built your project?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Clement",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37b89618981b80a0caaf7d4b1ce314974005bf49d3b6542218470df118511611",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37b89618981b-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Again, the rules that the Respondent has adopted since 1975 have specifically excluded the Nundane ditch, as well as the drain next to that ditch, as being defined as waters of the United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37b89618981b80a0caaf7d4b1ce314974005bf49d3b6542218470df118511611",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37b89618981b-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL CLEMENT: The Corps has not drawn a distinction between man-made channels or ditches and natural channels or ditches. And, of course, it would be very absurd for the Corps to do that since the Erie Canal is a ditch."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37b89618981b80a0caaf7d4b1ce314974005bf49d3b6542218470df118511611",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37b89618981b-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: I suggest it's very absurd to call that waters of the United States. It's a drainage ditch dug -- you know, dug by the municipality or -- you know, or a gutter in a street. To call that waters of the United States seems to me extravagant."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37b89618981b80a0caaf7d4b1ce314974005bf49d3b6542218470df118511611",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37b89618981b-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL CLEMENT: The two points I would make is, first of all, I think the Corps' regulations, which for 30 years have ignored the premise -- the -- the presence of a berm, are rational because in the vast, vast majority of cases, that berm is not going to prevent a hydrological connection, so to speak."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37b89618981b80a0caaf7d4b1ce314974005bf49d3b6542218470df118511611",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37b89618981b-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: No. I was referring to a real storm drain. (Laughter.)"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37b89618981b80a0caaf7d4b1ce314974005bf49d3b6542218470df118511611",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37b89618981b-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL CLEMENT: That's right. It's an undefined term. The Corps has interpreted it in the 2000 preamble."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Clement",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37b89618981b80a0caaf7d4b1ce314974005bf49d3b6542218470df118511611",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37b89618981b-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What I'm up here asking for is a recognition that the tributary system is something that Congress can validly regulate and did regulate in its broader definition of waters of the United States in the Clean Water Act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37b89618981b80a0caaf7d4b1ce314974005bf49d3b6542218470df118511611",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37b89618981b-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It's a very vague indication. I mean, I -- I agree with you that your argument based on 404(g) is a strong one, but it -- it perhaps is weakened if you believe that in order to stretch to the -- to the limit of Federal jurisdiction, you need a clear statement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Clement",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37b89618981b80a0caaf7d4b1ce314974005bf49d3b6542218470df118511611",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37b89618981b-0004-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What I would say, though, is that this case has just not framed up the question of tributaries, and that's because -- I mean, to put it more favorably to my client, the other side has never taken issue with the fact that their wetlands are adjacent to tributaries."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Clement",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37b89618981b80a0caaf7d4b1ce314974005bf49d3b6542218470df118511611",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37b89618981b-0004-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The last thing, I would say a couple of points before I sit down. I do think, first, that section 404(g) of the statute is very important because it is the clearest textual indication that Congress intended to regulate something beyond traditional navigable waterways and their adjacent wetlands."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37b89618981b80a0caaf7d4b1ce314974005bf49d3b6542218470df118511611",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37b89618981b-0004-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 76,
        "start": 76
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Hopper, I hope you're going to tell us what you make of section 404(g)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37b89618981b80a0caaf7d4b1ce314974005bf49d3b6542218470df118511611",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37b89618981b-0004-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 77,
        "start": 77
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We're told that one of them was much closer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Solicitor General",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "37b89618981b80a0caaf7d4b1ce314974005bf49d3b6542218470df118511611",
      "evidence_id": "ev-37b89618981b-0004-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 78,
        "start": 78
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Solicitor General represented to us that it was very close."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
